cat - print files

SYNOPSIS
    cat [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
    Writes each file to standard output, in order. With no files, or with -,
    copies standard input - which is what makes `cat` the thing at the front
    of a pipeline.

    A directory is refused rather than printed. Its blocks are entries, not
    contents, and handing them over as data produces something that looks
    like a corrupt file rather than an answer.

SEE ALSO
    less, head, tail, tee
